# Data integrity (non-negotiable)

**ALWAYS USE REAL DATA. NEVER FAKE OR MAKE UP ANY DATA.**

Canonical detail: `docs/DATA_INTEGRITY.md` and `project.md` → Data integrity.

## Must follow on every task

- Every user-visible number, pin, score input, listing, map marker, dining venue, flight path, and PDF link must come from a **real source** (NYC Open Data / Supabase, Google Places, Yelp, Mapbox, ADS-B ingest, etc.).
- **No invented records** — do not place pins, counts, or incidents that are not in fetched datasets.
- **No synthetic map fallbacks** — no heuristic flight corridors, random jitter, or demo swarms when live data is missing; show **nothing** or label **unavailable**.
- **Unavailable means unavailable** — empty / `unavailable` / graceful degrade; never approximate without clear labeling.
- **Truncation must be honest** — if the UI shows a subset of real locations, say so (e.g. “Showing 100 of N real locations”); scoring still uses full in-radius counts.
- **PDF / external links** — every dossier URI must open a **real filtered** official/source page — never a site homepage and never a localhost proxy.

## Allowed (display-only, not new facts)

- Great-circle / visual smoothing of **existing** ADS-B vertices for map rendering.
- Merged label when multiple **real** records share one NYC geocode.

## When unsure

Prefer **unavailable / empty / omit** over inventing. If a feature needs demo-looking output, use an explicit labeled mode only when product docs already define it (e.g. `FLIGHT_MODE=static`) — never as a silent fallback for `auto` / live paths.
